\[
-4A\,2^{n}-3B\,3^{n}-5C=-4\cdot2^{n}-3\cdot3^{n}+5,
\]

hence \(A=1,\;B=1,\;C=-1\).  
The homogeneous solution is \(C\cdot6^{\,n-1}\).  
Using \(a_{1}=10\) we obtain \(C=6\).

Thus for every \(n\ge 1\)

\[
\boxed{\,a_{n}=6^{\,n}+2^{\,n}+3^{\,n}-1\,}.
