We need an extra \(D=2025-2019=6\).  
Increase the largest even number \(50\) by \(6\) to obtain \(56\).  
The even set becomes  

\[
\{2,4,\dots ,48,56\},
\]

the odd set remains \(\{1,3,\dots ,73\}\).  
All numbers are distinct, the parity condition holds, and the total sum is exactly \(2025\).

Thus the pair \((m,n)=(25,37)\) is indeed feasible.

