            def find_periodic(d, max_val):
                # sequence of length d, repeated.
                # We'll define a list a[0..d-1]; for any n, a_n = a[n % d]
                # Condition must hold for all p up to some bound, but due to periodicity, we can check for p in 0..d-1 and also need to ensure that indices a_p, a_{a_p}, etc. are handled modulo d.
                # Since a_p may be any non-negative integer, but we only have values defined for residues. So we need to define a for any integer, using periodic extension.
